[style name="VisualNovelStyle"]
[signal arg="date_start"]
[background arg="res://Assets/CGs/BG_Ending.png" fade="1.5" wait="true"]
audio Musicly "res://Assets/Music/M_Date_ada.ogg" [fade="2.0" volume="-30.0" bus="Music" sync="Musicly"]
Narrator: You and Ada head out to the hottest club in town!
audio Musicly "res://Assets/Music/M_Date_ada.ogg" [fade="2.0" volume="-15.0" bus="Music" sync="Musicly"]
[background scene="res://Scenes & Scripts/CG Scenes/ada_date_cg.tscn" fade="1.5" wait="true"]
Narrator: They're fun and prettier than in their photos. Not a single lie about them being the life of the party was told.
Ada: Wooo!
Ada: I love this song!
Ada: Let's dance until we drop!
Ada: You better keep up okay? I want to party all night!
Narrator: The energy they carry is electric.
Narrator: While the sparkle of their dress and the body glitter isn’t the only thing that keeps your eyes on them all night, they certainly do help.
Narrator: They clearly feel the spark since they dance close to you all night.
Narrator: You both dance, you twirl them, their dress catching the light.
Ada: Two cosmos please!
Ada: You’ll looove the Cosmos here, they’re so good!
Narrator: She handed you the drink once they arrived, clinking their glass against yours.
audio "res://Assets/SFX/SFX_GlassClink.wav" [bus="Audio"]
Narrator: You pretend to drink as much as they do, watching them down pretty sunset colored drinks all night, waiting patiently until they reach their limit.
Narrator: Once they’re ready to go home, probably a little more drunk than they usually let themselves get, you are quick to offer a ride. They giggle roughly.
Ada: You are sooo sweet…
Narrator: And you simply reply that you were more than happy to take care of them.
audio Musicly - [fade="1.5" volume="-5.0" bus="Music"]
[background arg="res://Assets/CGs/BG_Ending.png" fade="1.5" wait="true"]
Narrator: They accept and you get them to your car with ease… The ride back is quiet, with Ada falling asleep in your seat.
Narrator: You carry them inside, under the cover of darkness.
Narrator: You were hungry.
Narrator: You pull out soy sauce, vinegar, onion, garlic, ginger, oyster sauce, bay leaves and various seasonings. Everything you needed except the main ingredient…
Narrator: You glance over at the octopus then at the clock. The marinade for this dish took a while so you should do it now.
Narrator: Your knife cuts into flesh with no struggle, thanks to the alcohol.
Narrator: You let the meat sit while you get everything else ready so the flavor really soaks into the flesh. You moved around the kitchen, chopping, washing rice.
Narrator: When it was time, you threw your prepared ingredients into a frying pan, waiting for the aromatics to start filling the kitchen.
Narrator: You add the octopus ink, letting it simmer and blanching the octopus so you could add it once the sauce was reduced Perfect.
Narrator: Poor Ada, bright and soft Ada.
Narrator: The Octopus Aquakin who shone like a bright flame, smothered too soon… But at least you got a delicious dinner out of them, right?
audio "res://Assets/SFX/SFX_Cooking_Ada.wav" [bus="Audio"]
[wait time="25.0"]
[background arg="res://Assets/CGs/BG_dinner_1.png" fade="3.5" wait="true"]
set {is_fdate_success} = true
set {is_date_success} = true
[signal arg="scene_end"]
[end_timeline]